+# Rental API specification
+
+## Purpose
+
+Provide the booking desk with an in-memory catalogue and booking service for boards and sails.
+This specification implements the rental-module requirement: register equipment, quote whole-day
+rentals, and book equipment while preventing overlapping reservations.
+
+## Public API
+
+`createRentalService()` creates an isolated service instance. It exposes:
+
+- `addEquipment(item)`: register `{ id: string, kind: 'board' | 'sail', dailyPrice: number }`.
+- `quote(request)`: return `{ itemId, start, end, total }` for `{ itemId, start, end }`.
+- `book(request)`: reserve an available item and return `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+
+All money values are integer euro cents. Item identifiers must be non-empty strings; equipment kinds
+must be `board` or `sail`; daily prices must be nonnegative safe integers. Re-adding an identifier is
+invalid. A period uses ISO-8601 UTC timestamps at midnight (`Z`), with `start < end`; it represents the
+half-open interval `[start, end)`, so `end` is the midnight after the last rental day. The total is the
+daily price multiplied by the number of days and must remain a safe integer.
+
+Unknown equipment, invalid data or periods, and an overlapping booking cause an error. Quotes do not
+reserve availability and may be returned even when another booking exists. Bookings for the same item
+may touch at their boundaries but may not overlap. Booking identifiers are unique within a service and
+assigned in creation order.
+
+The future cancellation policy is full refund at least 24 hours before a booking starts and no refund
+inside 24 hours. Cancellation is outside this API's current scope; no wall clock is consulted.
+
+## Decision
+
+The service uses private in-memory maps and a monotonically increasing booking sequence. This keeps
+instances isolated and deterministic without adding a runtime dependency or persistence coupling.
